# Ultimate BLT

Based on [https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/…](https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/blt) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20250910115023/https://www.cookwell.com/recipe/blt)) and [https://fieldcompany.com/blogs/…](https://fieldcompany.com/blogs/journal/how-to-cook-bacon-in-a-cast-iron-skillet) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251228112702/https://fieldcompany.com/blogs/journal/how-to-cook-bacon-in-a-cast-iron-skillet))

{ rating="5" image="ultimate_blt.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 2 slices[/sandwich bacon]{ ing="sandwich-bacon" } (look for no sugar added)
- [ ] [Sandwich bread]{ ing="sandwich-bread" }
- [ ] [Tomato]{ ing="tomato" }
- [ ] [Romaine lettuce]{ ing="romaine-lettuce" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] [Mayonnaise]{ ing="mayonnaise" }, spoonful
- [ ] [Pickled Onions]{ ing="pickled-onions" }
- [ ] [Vinegar]{ ing="vinegar" }, splash
- [ ] [Salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }

## Recipe

1. [Bacon]{ ing="sandwich-bacon" }

   1. Place 4-5 slices on an unheated skillet
   1. Heat on medium high until brown on one side (~5 min)
   1. Flip with tongs and cook until crispy (4-6 min)
   1. Place on a plate with a paper towel
1. Slice the [tomato]{ ing="tomato" } into 1/2” thick pieces. Sprinkle with [salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" } and let sit for 10 min
1. Finely slice the [lettuce]{ ing="romaine-lettuce" }
1. Toast the [bread]{ ing="sandwich-bread" }, add mayo, lettuce, [pickled onions]{ ing="pickled-onions" }, splash of [vinegar]{ ing="vinegar" }, bacon, and tomatoes
